 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, you are rolling two 6-sided dice, each of which has 3 orange faces, 2 green faces, and 1 blue face.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 516695,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the probability of rolling 2 orange faces?\n\n\n\n\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Blue</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>On both rolls, you have 3 orange sides out of 6 sides.</p>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(orange and orange) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{6}\\left( {\\frac{3}{6}} \\right) = \\frac{9}{{36}} = \\frac{1}{4}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{4}\">\\frac{1}{4}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516696,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the probability of rolling 2 green faces?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Blue</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>On both rolls, you have 2 green faces out of 6 sides.</p>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(green and green) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{6}\\left( {\\frac{2}{6}} \\right) = \\frac{4}{{36}} = \\frac{1}{9}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{9}\">\\frac{1}{9}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 516697,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the probability of rolling 1 orange and 1 green face (in any order)?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Sample space:</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Orange</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Green</td>\n<td>Blue</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>You have 3 orange sides out of 6 sides.</p>\n<p>You have 2 green faces out of 6 sides.</p>\n<p>The Multiplication Rule for Probability: If <span data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span data-math=\"F\"></span> are events associated with the first and second stages of an experiment, then <span data-math=\"{\\text{P}}\\left( {E\\,{\\text{and}}\\,F} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ P}}\\left( E \\right){\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ P}}\\left( {F|E} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>P(orange and green) = <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{6}\\left( {\\frac{2}{6}} \\right) = \\frac{6}{{36}} = \\frac{1}{6}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{6}\">\\frac{1}{6}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
